{
  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "No supported, safe, coverage-preserving optimization applies to this workflow. P-LIT-GHA-CACHE (cache dependency downloads) is contraindicated because equivalent caching already exists: setup-node caches pnpm (node_modules) and a separate actions/cache entry restores the Playwright Chromium binary keyed on pnpm-lock.yaml. P-LIT-FAIL-FAST (cancel remaining matrix jobs) does not apply because there is a single `main` job and no matrix. P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT (bound jobs with a custom timeout) has measured evidence with success preserved, but its precondition requires a representative successful-duration history and a budget with headroom that avoids false timeouts; observed successful runs span roughly 2.4–13.4 minutes, while the evidence's 5-minute budgets came from much smaller workflows, so applying that limit here risks violating the contraindication that valid slow runs exceed the proposed limit, and no measured safe upper bound exists for this job. A timeout would also not shorten the observed successful runs, so it is not a supported time-saving change for this workflow. P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE (cancel superseded runs) is unsafe because the workflow publishes preview packages via pkg-pr-new publish, and canceling an in-progress run could interrupt publishing; required-check status is also unverified.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT", "P-LIT-FAIL-FAST", "P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE"]
}
